  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "UNICEF reports that over 332 children have been killed and 609 injured by the new Israeli military offensive across the Gaza Strip since the resumption of the war after the breakdown of the 2025 ceasefire. ((BBC News)) ((UNICEF))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Four people are killed, including Hassan Bdeir, a high-ranking Hezbollah official, and seven others are injured by an Israeli airstrike on a building in Dahieh, Beirut, Lebanon. ((Reuters)) ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Houthis claim that they shot down a U.S. military MQ-9 Reaper drone in Marib Governorate, Yemen. ((AP))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Russian ministry of defence says that Russian forces have captured Rozlyv in Donetsk Oblast, Ukraine. ((Al Arabiya))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "A small airplane goes missing and is later found crashed into a lake in Os outside of Bergen, Norway, leaving two onboard dead. ((Sunnmørsposten))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Seismic activity increases near Grindavík, Iceland, with the Icelandic Meteorological Office reporting that a volcanic eruption has occurred and a earthquake is being registered. People visiting the Blue Lagoon are being evacuated rapidly. ((The Watchers))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "At least 305 people are injured after a gas pipeline owned by Petronas explodes and ignites a fire in Putra Heights, Selangor, Malaysia. ((Malay Mail))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "The Chinese PLA Navy and Air Force conduct large-scale military exercises around Taiwan. At least 19 Chinese warships are deployed, including the aircraft carrier Shandong, marking its closest ever approach to the island. ((The Guardian)) ((Financial Times))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "U.S. Senator Cory Booker delivers the longest speech in United States Senate history, breaking the previous record set by Strom Thurmond in 1957. ((AP News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Science and technology",
      "text": "SpaceX successfully launches four humans to orbit over Earth’s poles, for the first time for a human spaceflight mission. The journey will last three to five days. ((The New York Times))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Sports",
      "text": "The 2025 FIDE Women's World Chess Championship match between Ju Wenjun and Tan Zhongyi is scheduled to take place from April 1 to 23, across two Chinese cities: Shanghai and Chongqing. ((ChessBase))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Houthis claim that they shot down a U.S. military-operated MQ-9 Reaper drone in Marib Governorate, Yemen. ((AP))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "U.S. missile strikes on Hodeidah, Yemen, hit a water management facility, killing at least four people, according to the Houthi-run Al-Masirah network. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The U.S. announces it is sending a second aircraft carrier strike group, the group, to the region. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Seismic activity increases near Grindavík, Iceland, with the Icelandic Meteorological Office reporting that a volcanic eruption has occurred and a earthquake is being registered. People visiting the Blue Lagoon are evacuated rapidly. ((The Watchers))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "A small airplane crashes into a lake in Os near Bergen, Norway, killing the two people onboard. ((Sunnmørsposten))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Science and technology",
      "text": "SpaceX successfully launches four humans into orbit over Earth’s poles for the first time for the human spaceflight mission Fram2. The journey will last three to five days. ((The New York Times))"
    }
